# Variant proof battle 2 of 6 — the Perch (docs/ENEMY_ROSTER.md).
# The question: what is the high ground worth when something else wants it?
#
# The Perch spawns one tile from a ledge and nothing is in range 3 of it, so round 1 is the climb:
# Move 2 pays the +1 entry cost exactly. From round 2 it shoots for 2 instead of 1, and it will not
# come down while anything is in range — the Archer's favourite tile is now a contested objective.
# A Lesser Grappler works the other side of the same idea: HighGround outranks even the Archer in its
# target preference, so whoever climbs gets yanked off — but only from 2 tiles, not 3.
#
# Deliberate lint: the board is 7x9, not 7x7. Both deploy zones have to sit outside range 3 of the
# spawn or the Perch shoots on round 1 and never bothers climbing, which is the one thing this
# battle exists to show.

id: nv-02-contested-ledges
number: 702
name: Contested Ledges
description: A Perch races you for the ridge and fires for 2 once it is up there. Take the high ground first or fight uphill all battle.

spawn p = Perch
spawn g = LesserGrappler

roster a: Archer, Vanguard
roster b: Threadcaster, Archer

board:
  ..Hp...
  .......
  .^.....
  ....BBB
  .......
  .......
  .....H.
  AA...^.
  AA.g...
